#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265648 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d81ed476-a3a2-57be-b7f0-4b2de132956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265650} {:answer/id #uuid "b553aac5-8d44-507e-85e2-483a7ca6ee2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265651} {:answer/id #uuid "08fbb1fa-cd53-52b6-8196-cc14538e4a8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265652} {:answer/id #uuid "820c3579-99cc-58ec-ad98-1a63743b7c86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265653} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe005c4-cf2b-5111-832b-c7b6225601ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81ed476-a3a2-57be-b7f0-4b2de132956d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265650} :answer-field/id #uuid "b47f6277-8c45-5320-8eb8-6b1acce1b2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "641c1e03-d0a1-58b9-b0a0-52b1bb02a882" :question/math-academy-id "q-120020" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72b7fefd-5832-5a10-88fe-941167df7f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256226} {:answer/id #uuid "7507e855-4c12-51a7-9a9f-ae6f5e8b92e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256227} {:answer/id #uuid "941450ca-b432-57e0-88da-4f3e57cded91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256228} {:answer/id #uuid "6a05b73c-5266-524e-942d-aa4fdaa77be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256229} {:answer/id #uuid "b579223d-8d16-53c6-9211-cd05c4c8fd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "941450ca-b432-57e0-88da-4f3e57cded91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256228} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce6d0c7-9a44-59bf-beba-79c56172cfc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256225}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2169c30-fb8b-5ed9-9ee8-c3820a8c3a72" :question/math-academy-id "q-120024" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c598e3d-8ec0-5060-9c46-6604a72abcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256240} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f8f370-5c53-58d5-b28a-3312eb2ef750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256241} {:answer/id #uuid "448580ff-e38e-57bf-9ca3-e7ce3176cf72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256242} {:answer/id #uuid "8f36e0c4-2cb1-5785-bcd9-afae4aaefa72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256243} {:answer/id #uuid "42f6c4eb-a87f-58bf-aef3-28ceb4c29ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c598e3d-8ec0-5060-9c46-6604a72abcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256240} :answer-field/id #uuid "e283ba02-233b-5f63-8318-1d0a3156c7ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "081c95ae-81cb-52c0-9684-47a33bf79aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120058" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d032966b-4326-5239-82b2-543689851176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057964} {:answer/id #uuid "082f5515-61c0-52b6-98dd-3cf04804524c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057965} {:answer/id #uuid "3063ffce-42c8-5f57-b38d-b2a0ed2ec943" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057966} {:answer/id #uuid "592b7b16-3a33-569c-8c42-8a26100174c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057967} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff11ef8-eff3-5dac-894d-c16811908e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "592b7b16-3a33-569c-8c42-8a26100174c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057967} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f8d7f8-a46b-5bf5-a43b-3840b02f762c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b22f045c-0b9c-53f1-b536-66fda02ca447" :question/math-academy-id "q-24361" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186328908 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05d612ff-c79f-57e5-8848-f245950c16b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d612ff-c79f-57e5-8848-f245950c16b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328910} :answer-field/id #uuid "36e1c06e-02b3-5eb3-bb38-89c94e3dba9f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92adad31-0676-5e5c-b234-81f262965d25" :question/math-academy-id "q-327771" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}.$\n\n$4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={15}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
